course: dictionary
lesson: 6856
title: Oven
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An oven is a box in the kitchen that gets very hot, and we use it for baking and cooking. Words can also mean something else. «It's like an oven in here!» does not mean there is a box in the room. It means the room is very hot.
explain: Read the words around a word to find its meaning. «The inside of the oven is hot enough to burn skin instantly.» The words hot enough to burn tell you an oven is much hotter than a room, so keep your hands away.
explain: Ask yourself: does this word mean the real thing, or something like it? Then try your meaning in the sentence. If «oven» means a very hot place, does the sentence still make sense? If yes, you have the right meaning.
fact: An oven is a box in the kitchen that gets very hot for baking and cooking.
fact: «It's like an oven in here!» means it is very hot, even when there is no oven at all.
fact: The inside of an oven is hot enough to burn skin instantly, so always use oven gloves.
fact: If you burn your skin, hold it under cool running water: a boy in Arizona did this for 20 minutes, because cooling stops the burn going deeper.
fact: Baking powder helps cakes rise: it traps gas that expands in the oven heat.
exercise: «It's like an oven in here!» What does oven mean in this sentence? | A cold room with a fridge | A kind of cake | A box in the kitchen for baking | *Very hot
exercise: «The inside of the oven is hot enough to burn skin instantly.» Find one word that shows the oven can hurt you. | *burn | box | kitchen | inside
exercise: «Cakes rise without yeast, using baking powder or whisked eggs to trap gas that expands in the oven heat.» What makes the gas expand? | The kitchen table | Cold water | Sugar in a bag | *The oven heat
test: A boy in Arizona touches a hot oven door and holds his hand under cool water for 20 minutes. Why does he do this? | To wash the oven | *Because cooling stops the burn going deeper | To make the burn go deeper | To make his hand warm
test: Ben says, «The classroom is an oven today.» What does he mean? | The classroom smells of cake | *The classroom is very hot | The classroom is baking bread | There is a real oven in the classroom
exam: What is the best way to check your meaning of a new word? | Ask for the sentence to be longer | Guess and move on without thinking | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Look only at the first letter
